cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "debt-verify: verifiable execution of sovereign debt restructuring clauses under data revision"
abstract: "A three-valued (Kleene K3) clause verifier that answers whether a contractual trigger fires over the published revision interval rather than at a point estimate. Split-conformal bands are calibrated on the revision record itself (n=37, leave-one-out coverage 0.946 at nominal 0.90); point-value verification is decisive on 84 of 84 evaluable cells, and requiring the decision to survive the band leaves 63 unsupported. Complexity trichotomy P / NP-hard / PSPACE-hard, cross-checked against z3."
authors:
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Yangyi
    affiliation: Georgetown University
repository-code: "https://github.com/ZhangYangyi03/debt-verify"
license: Apache-2.0
type: software
keywords: [sovereign debt, conformal prediction, three-valued logic, formal verification, IMF]
